          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On Sunday, April 15, 1979, around 10:45 PM, witnesses observed a bright point in the sky that was moving. When it stopped, it changed color while twinkling. The gendarmes called to the scene will observe a bright point, about the size of a star, moving slowly to the East. We lack information regarding the direction and altitude of observation, but it is likely an astronomical observation, perhaps Vega.",
